      "content": "It's probably a good idea to use the eye drops to soothe and protect your eye, especially since you may have incurred some irritation. Antibiotic eye drops, like the ones you have, can help prevent infections if the soap irritation is more severe. Just be sure to follow the instructions on the packaging and use a few drops at a time to avoid over-dosing. If the redness and discomfort persist or worsen, you may want to consider consulting a doctor for further guidance.",
